    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96-a1">

                <pb facs="0208" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg106"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Chargé
                        Lorillard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs, General Division of Commercial and
                                Consular Affairs, First Bureau</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to His Excellency Mr. Charles Page Bryan’s note of the 18th of last
                    July, I have the honor to communicate to you that His Majesty’s Government,
                    accepting the invitation of the Government of the United States of America, has
                    decided to be represented on the international commission which is to <pb
                        facs="0209" n="107" xml:id="pg107"/> meet at Shanghai, in January, 1909, to
                    study and propose means to combat the use of opium in the regions of the Far
                    East, and it is a subject which is the object of investigation by a commission
                    sitting in the colony of Macau since August of the current year.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wenceslau de
                    Lima.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
